# Pool Party v2 Frontend - local environment.
# Copy to .env.local and adjust. Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are exposed to the browser.

# App environment label.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# Public app origin (scheme + host, no trailing slash) used to build share / deep-link URLs
# (referral ?ref=, manager /m/<handle>, public /strategies/<id>) in src/lib/urls.ts (POO-735).
# Set per environment; unset falls back to the prod origin. Localhost keeps http:// (not forced https).
#   local: http://localhost:3000   dev (v2.dev): https://v2.dev.pool-party.xyz   prod: https://app.pool-party.xyz
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Mock mode: unset or "true" => mock data (safe default). Only the literal "false" opts into
# the real integrations (not wired yet). Matches src/lib/services/index.ts (`!== "false"`).
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_MODE=true

# SIWE EIP-4361 message (POO-376). Keep OFF until the pool-party-api EIP-4361 verification companion (POO-436) is live.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SIWE_EIP4361=false

# Target chain id (Base mainnet placeholder).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=8453

# Fallback locale: any locale from src/i18n/config.ts (11 today).
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_LOCALE=en

# Operation minimums (USD). Optional — defaults live in src/lib/config/operationMinimums.ts.
# Lower these per environment (e.g. .env.dev) to test flows with small amounts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MIN_AMOUNT_FOR_ADD_LIQUIDITY=10
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MIN_AMOUNT_FOR_CREATE_POOL=20
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MIN_COLLECT_USD=0.10       # min collectable yield; "0" disables the floor (dev uses 0.01)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feature flags — per-environment area gating. See docs/FEATURE_FLAGS.md and src/lib/features.
# Each accepts on/off (also true/false/1/0). Unset => the registry default shown below. The values
# here are the v1 PROD launch state: core areas + Rewards on, everything else off (dark-launched).
# Flip one on (e.g. in .env.local or a staging env) to reveal that area — no code change needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Core areas (on; nav-level kill-switch only — disabling is an incident-only action):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_HOME=on
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_PORTFOLIO=on
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_STRATEGIES=on
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_DEPOSIT=on
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_PROFILE=on
# Launched:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_REWARDS=on
# Dark-launched (off in v1 — built behind the flag):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_CARDS=off            # next area to build
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_SAVINGS=off
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_BUY_TOKENS=off
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_PREDICTIONS=off
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_PERPS=off
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_MANAGER_CONSOLE=off  # also requires the isManager role
# Pre-flight provisioning gate (inline in the op modals, not a route). Ships OFF everywhere,
# including local dev: set this to demo it. In real mode it reads live balances and quotes real
# Uniswap routes, so it also needs UNISWAP_API_KEY (POO-1042):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_PROVISIONING=on
# Investor asset-category filter on the Strategies Explore screen (a control on an already-launched
# surface, not a route). Off = today's Explore; on reveals the Bitcoin/Ethereum/Stablecoins/Altcoins/
# Meme coins multi-select (POO-830 PR2):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_STRATEGY_CATEGORY_FILTER=on
# Non-prod convenience: reveal every off area at once (ignored when NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=prod):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_ALL=on

# Windowed-list virtualization threshold (POO-660). Lists LONGER than this window (unmount off-screen
# rows); at or below it they render a plain .map(), identical DOM. Unset -> 500 (prod). Set a low
# value in non-prod to exercise the windowed path on a small dataset (needs the `virtualize` flag,
# which NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_ALL reveals in dev). Invalid/negative/float values fall back to 500.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VIRTUALIZE_THRESHOLD=5

# Google Tag Manager container id. When set, GTM and the Consent Mode default snippet load.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=

# Wallet integration (POO-194). Required when NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_MODE=false:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_CLIENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WC_PROJECT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pool-party-api access (POO-206). Server-only (NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC).
# The server-side API client (src/lib/api/client.ts) is imported by Server
# Actions / Server Components only and injects x-api-key on every request to
# pool-party-api. The browser never calls the API directly and never sees
# PP_API_KEY. Required when NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_MODE=false and API calls are needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PP_API_URL=https://api.poolparty.example
# PP_API_KEY=
# Legacy (v0.8.0) backend for legacy networks (Arbitrum / Base), POO-316. Optional: when unset,
# legacy networks fall back to PP_API_URL (single backend). The API key is shared (PP_API_KEY).
# PP_API_URL_LEGACY=https://legacy-api.poolparty.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Next.js Server Actions encryption key (POO-673). BUILD-TIME, server-only.
# MUST be a STABLE, base64 32-byte value SHARED by every deployer of a given env: `push_image.sh`
# reads it from .env.<env> and passes it to `next build` as a build-arg. Without it, Next generates
# a random key per build, so Server Action IDs ROTATE each deploy and any stale browser tab breaks
# with "Failed to find Server Action". Generate once with `openssl rand -base64 32`; keep it stable.
# DEV shared value (low-sensitivity dev env — safe to commit so all dev deploys use the same key):
NEXT_SERVER_ACTIONS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-32>
# PROD uses its OWN key from the prod secret store — NEVER the dev value above.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics indexer access (POO-207). Server-only (NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC).
# The server-side analytics client (src/lib/analytics-api/client.ts) is imported
# by Server Actions / Server Components only and reads points/tier/activity from
# the Data_Analytics_PoolParty indexer. Separate from pool-party-api (PP_API_URL)
# and from the GTM container (NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID). Controllers mount at root (no
# /api prefix). Required when NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_MODE=false and rewards/activity
# reads are wired.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANALYTICS_API_URL=https://analytics.poolparty.example

# Server-only secret (NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC) used to HMAC wallet addresses into a
# pseudonymous analytics user_id (POO-164: served by POST /api/analytics/user-id; consumed by
# AnalyticsIdentify -> useAnalytics, consent-gated). Generate 32+ random bytes, e.g.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Unset = analytics runs unidentified (no user_id, no crash). Set per environment, never in git.
# PP_ANALYTICS_USER_ID_SECRET=

# --- Deploy: image version --------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMAGE_VERSION is the immutable ECR tag scripts/push_image.sh pushes the built image under (in
# addition to :latest), for both dev and prod. The deploy host pins this tag and rolls back to a
# previous one. Bump at least a patch on every deploy (e.g. v0.0.1 -> v0.0.2). Not a NEXT_PUBLIC_
# var, so it is never baked into the client bundle. Falls back to `git describe` if unset.
# IMAGE_VERSION=v0.0.0

# --- Uniswap Trading API (POO-1027, Universal Funding epic) -------------------------------------
# UNISWAP_API_KEY authenticates the Trading API calls that power provisioning: same-chain swaps
# (/quote + /swap) and cross-chain bridging via Chained Actions (/plan). Sent as `x-api-key` from
# src/lib/uniswap/client.ts, which is `server-only`.
#
# SERVER-ONLY, deliberately: there is NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and there must never be one (ADR 0003).
# A NEXT_PUBLIC_ key would ship to every browser and still work perfectly in testing, which is what
# makes that mistake worth calling out here rather than trusting review to catch it.
#
# Because nothing is fetched from the client, no CSP `connect-src` entry for
# trade-api.gateway.uniswap.org is needed. If a change ever seems to require one, a call has moved
# to the browser and the secret boundary has been broken.
#
# Unset = provisioning plans fail with UNISWAP_KEY_MISSING; nothing else in the app is affected.
# UNISWAP_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Aqua / Active Reserve (POO-1057 hackathon branch, server-only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AQUA_VAULT_ADDRESS: the PartyVault to display. NOT a secret: it is a deployed
# contract address, public and verifiable on Arbiscan, and the browser needs it to read a USDC
# allowance before depositing. NEXT_PUBLIC_ is baked at BUILD time, so changing the vault means
# a rebuild, not a restart.
#
# There is no database in this feature. Every value the page shows is read live from Arbitrum;
# the manager-written labels are committed in src/lib/aqua/data/managerMetadata.ts, which
# explains why at length.
#
# Unset = the Active Reserve page renders its empty state; the rest of the app is unaffected.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AQUA_VAULT_ADDRESS=

# ARBITRUM_RPC_URL: optional. Defaults to the public Arbitrum endpoint, which is fine for
# reads but rate-limited; set a private one before running the taker against mainnet.
# ARBITRUM_RPC_URL=

# TAKER_BOT_PRIVATE_KEY: the taker bot's own wallet, holding only its working capital.
# NEVER the manager or keeper key (BOT-R4). Manager transactions are returned as BuiltTx
# payloads for a human wallet to sign (SRV-R5), never signed server-side.
# Unset = the taker refuses to run; read-only paths still work.
# TAKER_BOT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# NEXT_PUBLIC_AQUA_VAULT_ADDRESS: the same vault address as AQUA_VAULT_ADDRESS, exposed to the
# browser on purpose. It is a public contract address, not a secret, and the client needs it to
# read the USDC allowance and decide whether the approve step can be skipped. Every transaction
# is still built by a server action; this is never used to construct calldata.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AQUA_VAULT_ADDRESS=

# AQUA_MANAGER_ADDRESS: the manager that owns the Active Reserve vaults. The frontend
# discovers strategies by scanning the Aqua registry for ships pointed at our router, then
# proves each maker is ours by checking OWNER() against this address. Public information;
# it is server-side only because nothing in the browser needs it.
# Unset = discovery is skipped and the page falls back to the single pinned AQUA_VAULT_ADDRESS.
# AQUA_MANAGER_ADDRESS=
